earch question, the key words, one synonym and a filled search plan using a new page of the invented catalog (rubric: key words fit, synonym tried, each try recorded); then four scenario cards, each answered with what to do and why (the safe-searching check). Tools: the invented catalog and results page, the library map, the scenario cards, the search plan sheet (Curio Class writes all). Host: a key-word search for the host question of ELA grade 3 unit 2 (days 40 to 77), the frogs research (e3-short-research), or for the science grade 3 unit 2 (days 17 to 33) magnets question; stand-alone: "What is on the far side of the moon?" | After unit 1 because a search needs a research question to pull key words from; before unit 3, which needs a found source in hand; safe searching sits with the first search so the stop rule is in place before any device day a school adds | Candidate: the continuum's grade 3 cells on bookmarked or teacher-chosen sites over free searching, as the reason the inquiry day uses a closed list; locating nonfiction at a readable level, as the second line of the search plan | The stop rule: the teacher page says what the adult does if an upsetting result ever appears on a screen (close it, the child tells, no blame) and points to health's steps if a child tells something worrying (APPROACH.md, Section field 1). No student types personal details, even on a pretend card. Searches use the closed catalog or a teacher-checked list only. Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its catalog entries and passages (C12) |
