"""Stale-note catch (added 2026-11-13): notes that say a piece of work is not done yet go stale the moment it is.

    python -X utf8 scripts/stale.py check [file ...]

A note that waits on other work carries a marker the checker can test:

    Pending(<what>): <the note>

where <what> is one of
- a file path from the repository root: resolved once the file exists;
- path#text: resolved once that file contains the text (Pending(data/standards/x.txt#RST.11-12.8));
- a plan-flow node id (frame:science:5, prog-review:all): resolved once data/plans/flow-status.csv marks it done.

FAIL: a Pending marker whose work has landed (the note is stale: rewrite it to say what is now true and drop the
marker); a Pending marker naming no file, text or node the checker knows the form of; a work-status phrase
("not yet placed", "until it is added", "to come", "TBD", "placeholder" and the like) outside a Pending marker
(mark it so the checker can follow it, or reword it).
Teaching boundaries ("not yet describe", "not yet measured with a ruler") are about the student, not the work, and
are not flagged. With no files, checks the four progressions and the course frames (docs/courses/**/*.md,
data/frames/*.csv when they exist).
"""
import csv
import glob
import os
import re
import sys

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
MARK = re.compile(r'Pending\(([^)]*)\)\s*:')
# Work-status wording: says something about our own unfinished work. Kept narrow so a student boundary
# ("not yet describe") never trips it.
WORK = re.compile(
    r"not yet (in the|placed|written|built|added|loaded|in a curio class|named by|decided|chosen)"
    r"|until (it|they|this|that|the [\w ,'-]{1,40}) (is|are) (added|written|built|loaded|placed|decided|chosen)"
    r"|once (it|they|the [\w ,'-]{1,40}) (is|are|exists?) (added|written|built|loaded|placed|decided)"
    r"|\b(?:yet|still|is|are) to come\b|\bTBD\b|\bTODO\b|placeholder|will be (placed|written|added|decided)"
    r"|held here in words", re.I)
_done = None


def done_nodes():
    global _done
    if _done is None:
        _done = set()
        p = os.path.join(ROOT, 'data', 'plans', 'flow-status.csv')
        if os.path.exists(p):
            for r in csv.DictReader(open(p, encoding='utf-8')):
                if r.get('state') == 'done':
                    _done.add(r['node'])
    return _done


def resolved(what):
    """True if landed, False if still waiting, None if the target is not a form the checker knows."""
    what = what.strip()
    path, _, text = what.partition('#')
    if '/' in path or '.' in os.path.basename(path):
        f = os.path.join(ROOT, path)
        if not os.path.exists(f):
            return False
        if not text:
            return True
        return text in open(f, encoding='utf-8', errors='replace').read()
    if ':' in what or re.fullmatch(r'P\d+[a-z]?', what):
        return what in done_nodes()
    return None


def check_text(label, text):
    """Fails for one note. Work-status wording inside a Pending clause (up to the next sentence end) is fine."""
    fails = []
    covered = []
    for m in MARK.finditer(text):
        r = resolved(m.group(1))
        if r is None:
            fails.append('%s: Pending(%s) names no file, file#text or plan node' % (label, m.group(1)))
        elif r:
            fails.append('%s: STALE, Pending(%s) has landed; rewrite the note to say what is now true' % (label, m.group(1)))
        end = text.find('. ', m.end())
        covered.append((m.start(), len(text) if end < 0 else end + 1))
"""The one gate command (consolidation 4.G).

    python -X utf8 scripts/gate.py --course <id>     the course's gates; new lines against its stored baseline
    python -X utf8 scripts/gate.py --changed         the gates of every course the uncommitted changes touch, plus
                                                     the shared ones (and the self-tests if a script changed)
    python -X utf8 scripts/gate.py --all [--site]    every gate; --site also builds the site into the run folder
                                                     and runs check_site.py on it
    add --record to a --course run of a committed course to write its failing count to data/plans/debt.csv (the
    lead, at each grade close; 4.L).
    add --baseline to store this run as the scope's baseline (build/gates/base-<scope>/, ignored). A --course run
    stores it by itself whenever the course has nothing uncommitted, refuses --baseline on a changed course, and
    fails (exit 2) on a changed course with no baseline. A --course run prints failing counts by gate and rule and
    only the new lines; add --verbose to list every failing line.
    add --save <name> to keep the run as build/gates/<name>/ with docs/reviews/consolidation/<name>/summary.csv
    python -X utf8 scripts/gate.py compare <a> <b>   new lines in run b against run a (folder names under build/gates)
    python -X utf8 scripts/gate.py list [--course <id> | --changed | --all]

Per course: plan.py check, lesson_course.py, unitplan.py check, ledger.py check for its subject, frame.py check, the
index reports (scripts/index.py) and lint (scripts/lint.py) for the course. --all adds ledger.py files, rows.py
check, the marker guard, sequence.py check, the self-tests (the skeletons, rows.py, safe_write.py, ledger.py,
index.py), lesson.py check, front_office.py check, check_tools.py, check_safety.py, tool_stages.py check,
tool_record.py check, board.py, course_status.py and
desk_stats.py. board.py and course_status.py rewrite docs/BUILD-BOARD.md and docs/COURSES-STATUS.md; commit or
restore them.

The compare prints, gate by gate, every line that is new (no cap in the stored file), and flags a gate that
disappeared, an exit code that changed and a count of failing lines that rose (a count that fell is reported once).
A new line fails when it is a FAIL line or a lint line; anything else new is shown as a note. The exit code is 1 when
anything fails, so turn.py, the lead, coursegen's gate lines and the consolidation runner all read one answer.
Output lines that only carry timings are dropped before comparing.
"""
