84: **Ownership** (ours, untested). Each of the 68 ids is owned by exactly one grade, the school year where it is first
85: met at the depth a check can score on its own (not the "with help" level); every other year where a course returns
86: to it carries `~ID` with a one-line note on how that year differs. Grades 6 to 8 and 9 to 12 get a progression row
87: per school year (6, 7, 8; 9, 10, 11, 12) even though each is one course: the progression's grades are the school
88: years, the course is how they are taught. Each row's `assumes` names only the earlier library row it builds on
