134: | Id | Receiving subject and course band | Why there |
135: |---|---|---|
136: | V.B.1 | Science, K to 12: the engineering design rows and the `design-cycle` model (from `sk-define-problem`, K-2-ETS1-1) | The design, test and improve cycle is engineering design, which science teaches every year; computer science uses the same loop |
137: | V.A.1 | ELA, K to 12: the range of reading and writing rows (RL and RI .10, W.10: `ek-group-reading`, `e3-reading-range` onward, `e3-writing-tasks` onward) | Reading widely in many forms and writing for many purposes is ELA's own range standard |
138: | V.D.1 | SEL, all four bands (`sel-k-2` to `sel-9-12`): SM3, keeping on task and pushing yourself | Trying again when a task gets hard is self-management, taught on everyday cases |
139: | V.D.2 | SEL, all four bands: SA8, skill grows with effort, practice and help | The growth view of skill is a self-awareness sub-skill |
140: | III.D.2 | SEL, all four bands: RS4, working as a team | Treating the group's learning as one's own job is a teamwork skill, taught where SEL teaches teams |
141: 
142: - **What a school may swap or leave out** (Cory, 2026-11-21, Desk q-fix-library-1; the same rule as SEL, PE and
143:   arts, docs/courses/arts/STANDARD.md section 5): a school or family may swap a case or leave out a unit for its
144:   community's reasons. Swapping a case for another keeps the unit's ids met; leaving out a unit means the course page
145:   and the unit's family note name the ids not claimed that year. K to 5 case sets stay neutral: no politics,
146:   elections, religion, identity groups or conflict (APPROACH.md, "Sensitive ground", item 1).
