stions can be answered by finding information (the teacher's sort, said aloud) | Neutral topics only (frogs, owls, places on a map). A "person who knows" is a school staff member by job, never a family member, and no child is asked who at home knows things. A child who writes slowly may say the "because" to the teacher, who writes it (a scribe, APPROACH.md section field 9). Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its read-aloud, pages and pictures (C12) |
