ges; maker and purpose for three invented pages), inquiry (the cycle on the host or stand-alone question: facts from two sources into the boxes, the fact that differs, a third source checked, the maker of each source named; credit lines; share; self-check), end-of-unit assessment, respond (it opens with the class box mat shared and the self-check, about five minutes, then the regrouped reteach). Skill card: "sort it, spot the difference, check a third, who made it and why?" pictured. End-of-unit evidence (about 15 minutes for 30): a sheet item: four new fact cards cut and glued into two or three boxes on a mat (g2-fact-sort, about 5 minutes, marked from the page: each card in a fitting box); a sheet item: two short passages read aloud that disagree on one fact; the child circles the two facts and ticks "check a third source" (g2-two-books-differ, about 5 minutes); a sheet item: an invented book cover and an invented page, and for each the child circles who made it and why, teach, story or sell (g2-who-made-it, about 4 minutes). Tools: fact cards, box mats, paired passages, invented pages on paper, the turtle read-aloud, the five-picture cycle card (Curio Class writes them all). Host: what plants need, s2-plant-needs-test in science grade 2 unit 5 (days 48 to 56), taught in the same weeks; or where water is found, s2-water-where in science grade 2 unit 1 (days 1 to 10), as review; stand-alone: "How long does a turtle live?" | After unit 2 because the class can now find and credit two books, so it can compare them; the three moves share one find step on one case set, so they are taught together as the cycle's new "check" picture. Placed in weeks 15 to 20, beside science's plant needs unit and social studies' two accounts (unit 5), and after social studies' source makers and ELA's author's purpose, so the maker question meets words the class has heard | Candidate: the continuum's grade 2 cells on recognizing that not all information on the internet is true (said on the