tes for 30): from a new broad topic and a short overview passage, a narrowed part, two or three questions with a predicted answer, and a plan whose sources fit its questions (rubric); then a search plan for one of the questions across two of three new printed kinds, saying what each was good for (rubric). Tools: the Arctic overview passage, the three printed kinds, the plan sheet and search plan (Curio Class writes all). Host: the neighboring-country research of social studies grade 4 unit 2 (days 17 to 38) (ss4-canada-mexico-research), on its land, climate and animals; stand-alone: "How do Arctic animals get through the winter?" | First because every later unit starts from a plan and a search across kinds; the weeks fit social studies grade 4's research project on a neighboring country, which needs a narrowed part and a plan | Candidate: the continuum's grade 4 cells on recognizing gaps in what one knows and stating what is known from an overview, at the plan's first line; following a template and a timeline, as the plan sheet | The host keeps to land, climate, animals and places; no question about a people, a culture or a border issue (K to 5 neutral rule). Searches use the printed kinds or a teacher-checked page under the stop rule (APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground, item 2). Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its sources (C12) |
