akers); day 4, a source list line for one cover (g3-source-list). Days: show-me (answer-only notes and one's own categories), show-me (primary and secondary on the same topic; purpose and the ad), show-me with practice (honest use: own words, a short quotation, credit; sort and fix four cases), practice (notes from a new passage into own boxes; four invented pages sorted by purpose), inquiry (notes from a primary and a secondary source for the host question into the student's own boxes, a source list, a pair share, the self-check), end-of-unit assessment, respond. Skill card: "question beside me, answer only, my words, my boxes; first-hand or about it, why made; my words, a few in marks, say where". End-of-unit evidence (written sitting, about 27 minutes for 30): a new passage and question, notes that keep only the answers, in own words, sorted into the student's own labeled boxes with the plan said (rubric, about 12 minutes); one line on what a new primary and a new secondary source can each tell, and three invented pages sorted by purpose with the ad marked (items, about 7 minutes); two not-yet-honest cases fixed with a reason (rubric, about 8 minutes). Tools: the beaver source set (a wildlife worker's field log, a photo with caption, two book passages), four invented pages, the honest-use case cards (Curio Class writes all). Host: the energy resources question of science grade 4 unit 2 (days 16 to 38) (s4-energy-resources), or the animal defenses research of ELA grade 4 unit 2 (days 39 to 77) (e4-research), in the same weeks; stand-alone: "What do beavers do to a stream when they build a dam?" | After unit 1 because a plan and a search have put sources in hand, and notes must now keep only what answers the plan's questions; honest use sits with note-making, where copying starts; before unit 3, whose records and unit 4's sheet are built from such notes | Candidate: the continuum's grade 4 cells on facts, details and inferences that support a main idea and a conclusion drawn from evidence, at the notes step; noting where two sources differ, as one line of the inquiry day | Honest use without shaming (APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground, item 4): a student whose notes copy a sentence is helped privately to put it in their own words and cite, never named in front of the class. Social studies grade 4 unit 4 uses primary sources on voyages and conquest; library borrows only the primary and secondary idea and runs on beaver cases (K to 5 neutral rule). The ad page sells an invented product with no brand. Whose voices: the unit records the makers of its sources (C12) |
